UID:event_317482580@meetup.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261130T120000
SEQUENCE:1
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261122T144338Z
DESCRIPTION:Triangle Off Road Cyclists (TORC)\nWe’ll focus on refreshing
  and shaping the bumps and features near the beginning of the outer loop\,
  using guidance from Rob McCaskill\, TORC’s Little River Trail Coordinat
 or and an experienced jump/flow feature builder.\n\n* Duration: No more th
 an 2.5 hours\n* Type of work: Moving dirt\, shaping existing features\, cl
 earing brush\, and other trail work as needed\n* We’ll provide tools and
  cold drinks.\n* Bring sturdy shoes or boots\, gloves\, appropriate clothi
 ng\, and water.\n\nPlease sign the 2026 TORC waiver if you haven’t alrea
 dy. You only need to sign it once per calendar year:\nhttps://www.webscore
 r.com/register?raceid=415052\n\nNever volunteered for a trail workday? No 
 problem. We’ll show you how to use the tools properly and safely.\n\n**M
 eetup location**: Meet at the Haley’s Branch / 286 trailhead on Old Reed
 y Creek Rd. at 11:45 AM for check-in and a safety talk. Dirt parking at th
 e trailhead is limited. You can also park in the paved Old Reedy Creek Roa
 d Trailhead lot at 2139 Old Reedy Creek Rd.\n\nRain or wet trail condition
 s may force us to cancel. Check Meetup for updates.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261122T144338Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://www.meetup.com/torc-nc/events/317482580/
X-SOURCE:Triangle Cycling
END:VEVENT
