DTSTAMP:20261128T073114Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54551646059606
DTSTART:20261214T000000Z
DTEND:20261214T013000Z
DESCRIPTION:Every year\, the Earth travels through a debris field left behi
 nd by a Sun-orbiting asteroid resulting in an amazing meteor shower that l
 ight up the mid-December skies. Join a Ranger to learn about these and oth
 er fiery space objects and then enjoy the show!\n\nAll children must be ac
 companied by an adult. Please be sure to dress appropriately for the weath
 er\, bring water\, chairs\, and a blanket!\n\nSpaces are limited\, and reg
 istration is required. To sign up\, call (984) 250-1370 or email eno.river
 @ncparks.gov. Include the number of guests in your party and a phone numbe
 r where you can be reached if the event is changed or canceled.
GEO:36.078519;-79.005129
LOCATION:Eno River State Park - Fews Ford Access & Visitor Center\, Loop Pa
 rking Lot (End of the Road)
SUMMARY:Winter Stargazing: The Geminids
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/winter-stargazing-the-gemini
 ds
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
END:VEVENT
