BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_41d85e1478a55e3b4adbf2e4951c5be9f6e49241ac55a65427c71d252849bf1c
SUMMARY:Defend Democracy Saturdays: Downtown Durham
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T113000
DTSTAMP:20261128T073051Z
UID:7vihpmeg1k6esqp5s5vsvq9hfe_R20260110T150000@google.com__20261219
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20251010T141601Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Please join Engaged Defenders for Democracy every Saturday 
 from 10am-11:30am with signs to protect our democracy and protest the viol
 ations to our Constitution. We will meet at the YMCA at 218 West Morgan St
 .</p><p>We need to fight for our democracy and stop and prevent future cut
 s that are hurting many. Bring friends! Bring signs that show your concern
  or are a call to action. Please avoid triggering images like swastikas.</
 p><p>See you every Saturday morning engaging drivers &amp\; pedestrians in
  Downtown Durham!</p><p>Please join our Substack:<span> </span><a href="h
 ttps://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy">https
 ://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy</a></p><p>
 For more ED4D Mobilize Events:<span> </span><a href="https://www.mobilize
 .us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersf
 ordemocracy/</a></p><p><a href="https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfor
 democracy/event/842514/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocra
 cy/event/842514/</a> </p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260108T021307Z
LOCATION:218 W Morgan St\, Durham\, NC\, 27701
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (In Person)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncbg": "https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/coker-arboretum-tour/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncbg
X-SOURCE:NC Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T120000
DTSTAMP:20261120T162442Z
CREATED:20261120T160212Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261120T162442Z
UID:10000885-1797674400-1797681600@ncbg.unc.edu
SUMMARY:Tour of Coker Aboretum
DESCRIPTION:with Geoffrey Neal\, Curator\, Coker Arboretum \n  \nDiscover this five-acre gem in the heart of the UNC campus! Established in 1903\, Coker Arboretum is part of the North Carolina Botanical Garden and features a diverse collection of plants\, including flowering trees and shrubs\, bulbs\, and perennials. Join a Coker Arboretum curator for a winter walking tour and explore the history and beauty of this beloved garden. \nOffered each season\, every tour reveals something new as the Coker Arboretum changes throughout the year. \n  \nRegister here!\n  \nAccessibility:  \nThis is an outdoor tour that follows mostly flat pathways\, including brick and smooth or compacted grit surfaces.  After rains\, grit paths may become uneven\, eroded\, or soggy\, which may affect ease of travel. Participants are welcome to move at their own pace and take breaks as needed. We’ll be happy to discuss your needs and determine how we can best support your participation.
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/coker-arboretum-tour/
LOCATION:Coker Arboretum\, 399 E. Cameron Avenue\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
CATEGORIES:Hikes and Tours
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncbg.unc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/963/2026/11/112922_0305-scaled.jpg
GEO:35.9131808;-79.0483369
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Coker Arboretum 399 E. Cameron Avenue Chapel Hill NC 27514 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=399 E. Cameron Avenue:geo:-79.0483369,35.9131808
END:VEVENT
