DESCRIPTION:Listen along as a park ranger reads a series of childrens books
  by a fire at Mayo Mountains outdoor shelter. Books include "The Eagles ar
 e Back" by Jean Craighead George and "Every Autumn Comes the Bear" by Jim 
 Arnosk. Afterwards\, kids will be able to play with antique American toys 
 and games like "Nine Pins"\, "Cup and Ball"\, and "Dominos". \n\nWe are ho
 sting this in celebration of America 250 and the upcoming New Years. \n\nP
 lease click "Interested" so we know you are coming. Events are subject to 
 cancel if no one posts interest. Hot Chocolate and Coffee will be availabl
 e.
GEO:36.439192;-79.948638
LOCATION:Mayo River State Park - Main Access and Park Office\, Mayo Mountai
 n - Shelter
SUMMARY:Reading in the Park
