BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_enoriver_org_9u7o786v1jlk6heq5cp3k1gr1k
SUMMARY:ERA & ERSP: First Day Hike on the Eno
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270101T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270101T163000
DTSTAMP:20261128T073054Z
UID:4jjojno2b1g88jfc0fv8a7ol30@google.com__20270101
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20210803T152701Z
DESCRIPTION:Kick off the New Year with a hike on the Eno! An annual tradit
 ion that started in 1971\, hike alongside friends and family at Eno River 
 State Park to start the new year together.<br><b><br></b><br><b>When:</b>
  2:00pm on Friday\, January 1st 2027<br><b>Where: </b>Eno River State Par
 k\, Cox Mountain Trailhead\, 6101 Cole Mill Rd\, Durham NC<br><b>What to e
 xpect when you arrive: </b>The event begins at 2:00pm\, but please plan to
  arrive early as parking fills up closer to the start of the event. Park R
 angers and volunteers will be on-site to assist with parking. Please follo
 w their instructions. Check-in at the Eno River Association table located 
 at the end of the parking lot near the Fews Ford picnic shelter.<br><b>Hik
 es: </b>At 2:00pm\, gather in the Fews Ford picnic area at the Cox Mountai
 n Trailhead for a welcome message from the Eno River Association and Eno R
 iver State Park Superintendent. There will be two hike options led by a hi
 ke leader - a short hike along Buckquarter Creek Trail (about 2.5 miles) a
 nd a long hike along Cox Mountain Trail (about 4.5 miles). After completin
 g your hike\, join us for hot cocoa and conversation at the Fews Ford picn
 ic shelter back at the trailhead.<br><br>See you there!!
LAST-MODIFIED:20261028T133703Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-SOURCE:Eno River Association
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining-north-carolinas-black-heritage"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261128T073116Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53138242028626
DTSTART:20270101T150000Z
DTEND:20270101T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
  at the Gregg Museum of Art & Design presents a series of vignettes explor
 ing spaces of dignity\, belonging\, safety\, and imagination within Black 
 communities across North Carolina. Featuring historical photographs\, cont
 emporary images\, artworks from the Gregg Museum collection including a ha
 ndmade guitar by Freeman Vines\, and ephemera from community partners\, th
 e exhibition reflects on place\, memory\, creativity\, and spiritual resil
 ience across generations. Through stories of triumph and adversity\, Commu
 nity Stories honors the ways Black Americans have sustained and uplifted t
 heir communities through family\, entrepreneurship\, cultural expression\,
  and soulful imagination\, while inspiring future generations.
GEO:35.784925;-78.661662
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining
 -north-carolinas-black-heritage
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/hiking-through-history-at-vade-mecum"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261128T073116Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54567216533993
DTSTART:20270101T150000Z
DTEND:20270101T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Start your New Years off with a brisk 2-mile historical hike al
 ong the Vade Mecum trails. Your guide will take you through the decades as
  we walk through the old Camp Sertoma high ropes course\, and stroll along
  the Pelican Pool trail while learning more about the circus animals that 
 once overwintered here. We will cross over century old bridges and learn a
 bout the small town that was once set in these hills. See the spectacular 
 glimmering reflections at the Palisades as we visit the old Mineral Spring
 s\, whose water was once sold throughout North Carolina. Sites we will als
 o pass along the way are the outdoor amphitheater\, Diamond Lake Dam\, and
  the outdoor Chapel of Peace built by the Episcopalian Diocese. The hike w
 ill end with a glance of the Historic Vade Mecum Hotel and Chapel of Thank
 s as we hike past the property that will reopen to the public in 2027. Thi
 s hike is appropriate for adult adventures. Space is limited\; to register
  for this event and for more information please email andra-claire.greene@
 ncparks.gov.
GEO:36.415673;-80.303864
LOCATION:Vade Mecum Trail Center Parking  Lot 
SUMMARY:First Day Hikes: "Hiking Through History" at Vade Mecum 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/hiking-through-history-at-va
 de-mecum
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:First Day Hikes
END:VEVENT
