SUMMARY:ERA - Guided History Hike - Confluence Natural Area
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270110T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270110T160000
DTSTAMP:20261128T073054Z
UID:6o07s308gj20uk3pmhlq2g62bl@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20270110T140000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20261120T150522Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/guided-history-hike-c
 onfluence-natural-area-tickets-2005141648648?aff=oddtdtcreator" target="_b
 lank">Register here</a> - tickets will be released on Dec. 1\, 2026 at 12
 :01 AM</p><p>This 2.5-mile guided history hike will include the East and W
 est Forks of the Eno\, the confluence where the main stem of the Eno River
  begins. Learn about the history of the land and the people who inhabited 
 it\, from Indigenous people to the Sheppard family who owned the mill\, of
  which remnants can still be seen today. We will discuss our latest findin
 gs about the mill\, which we just learned more about this year!</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20261120T153825Z
LOCATION:Confluence Natural Area\, 4214 Highland Farm Rd\, Hillsborough\, 
 NC 27278\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Eno River Association
END:VEVENT
