BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Dwg Writers": "https://www.meetup.com/dwg-writers/events/khsdcvykccbjc/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_dwg_writers
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Durham Writers Group
UID:event_khsdcvykccbjc@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261128T073102Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270126T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270126T213000
SUMMARY:*IN-PERSON* SF/F Group
DESCRIPTION:Durham Writers Group\nWe will be at the Moon House at 3039 Uni
 versity Dr. in Durham. This venue does not serve food or drink\, but feel 
 free to bring your own. There is a kitchenette for our use\, but be sure t
 o clean up afterwards. The space might be a little cozy\; please consider 
 masking or staying home if you have a respiratory ailment.\n\nThis sub-gro
 up focuses on Speculative Fiction\, including Science Fiction\, Fantasy an
 d Horror. If you have anything that falls under that category — be it sh
 ort story\, poem\, novel-in-progress or screenplay — then come! We'd lov
 e to hear from you.\n\nOur format allows each reader 15 minutes to present
  their work aloud\, followed by approximately 20 minutes of feedback from 
 the other attendees. To ensure fairness\, each attendee is limited to 1 mi
 nute of Initial Feedback time. During that period\, the author remains sil
 ent. Next\, we have a 5 minute Free-For-All discussion about the work -- t
 hen the author may speak. (We usually get through three readers.)\n\nThoug
 h not required\, in order to receive more in-depth feed-back\, readers may
  post their work in advance on our Google Group:\nhttps://groups.google.co
 m/d/forum/durham-sff-writers-group\n\nWe ask that participants keep their 
 comments constructive and respectful\, focusing on what works or doesn't w
 ork in the piece.\n\nWe also ask that readers provide a warning\, both on 
 the Google Group and during the meeting\, if their story features content 
 that some readers might find upsetting. This includes descriptions of viol
 ence or sexual content.\n\nReaders are:\n•\n•\n•\n\nBackup Readers a
 re:\n•\n•\n•\n\nDeep Backup:\n•\n\n***\n\n***We meet every Tuesday
  at the same time\, but alternate between In-Person*** ***and on Zoom. Mem
 bers may attend both formats\, if desired\, but readers will be listed sep
 arately under the In-Person or Zoom weeks.***
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/dwg-writers/events/khsdcvykccbjc/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261124T191350Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261124T191350Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/introduction-to-qualtrics-714"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261128T073144Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54418725711083
DTSTART:20270126T190000Z
DTEND:20270126T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Qualtrics is a powerful browser-based web-survey tool. It is av
 ailable to UNC Chapel Hill faculty\, staff\, and students\, for UNC-relate
 d projects. Qualtrics allows users to build complex surveys\, distribute t
 hem\, and analyze the responses all from one place.\n\n \n\nIn this course
 \, we will cover basic Qualtrics functions beginning with an overview of s
 urvey options and settings\, followed by hands-on practice programming and
  distributing a survey and downloading results. We will program some of th
 e most common question and response types\, customize requirements and val
 idation\, and add display logic\, skip logic\, and basic branch logic in t
 he “survey flow”. We will then create and upload a contact list and di
 scuss advantages and disadvantages of distributing the survey with a singl
 e reusable link vs. the survey mailer.  Finally\, we will cover a basic ov
 erview of the Data & Analysis tab for viewing\, editing\, and exporting ra
 w data into various formats including .csv\, .tsv\, .excel\, and .spss. Ot
 her topics include project sharing/ collaboration\, Groups and Libraries\,
  and preventing fraudulent responses and bot activity.\n\n \n\nThis is an 
 introductory course and will not cover the online analysis tools within Qu
 altrics. Please note\, this is a hands-on\, online course. All participant
 s are required to create a Qualtrics account before the course. Carolina f
 aculty\, staff and students may create their free Qualtrics account here t
 o access full features: http://qualtrics.unc.edu. Non-UNC affiliated parti
 cipants can create a free trial account here: https://www.qualtrics.com/\n
 \n \n\nRegistration and fee (refundable for UNCCH students upon attendance
 ) are required for Zoom link access. This event is sponsored by the UNC Od
 um Institute for Research in Social Science
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Introduction to Qualtrics
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/introduction-to-qualtrics-714
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
