X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261128T073144Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54551210410502
DTSTART:20270206T150000Z
DTEND:20270206T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Interprofessional Design-a-thon brings together student tea
 ms to apply human-centered design thinking to address patient needs. Stude
 nt teams collaborate on a solution and present their idea to a panel of fa
 culty and health professionals\, who then select a winning team. This is a
 n approved IPEP Distinguished Scholars Immersion hosted by the Office of I
 nterprofessional Education and Practice.\n\n \n\nFall 2026 Design-a-thon:\
 n\nSaturday\, January 30 from 10 a.m. to 3 p.m.\n\nSaturday\, February 6 f
 rom 10 a.m. to 3 p.m.\n\n \n\nDesign-a-thon Eligibility:\n\nComplete basic
  BEAM Makerspace training.Be available all 5 hours on each Saturday (10 ho
 urs total) and complete independent work (research\, faculty consultation\
 , etc.) in the week between.Designed for medical\, nursing\, biomedical en
 gineering\, physical therapy\, clinical rehabilitation and mental health c
 ounseling\, occupational therapy\, speech therapy and pharmacy students. O
 ther students can apply\, and their participation will be considered as sp
 ace allows.​Applications are reviewed as received and the priority deadl
 ine to apply is December 1\, 2026. Questions? Email unc_ipe@unc.edu.
LOCATION:On Campus\, TBD
SUMMARY:Interprofessional Design-a-thon
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/interprofessional-design-a-tho
 n-2688
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining-north-carolinas-black-heritage"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261128T073117Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53138242048108
DTSTART:20270206T150000Z
DTEND:20270206T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
  at the Gregg Museum of Art & Design presents a series of vignettes explor
 ing spaces of dignity\, belonging\, safety\, and imagination within Black 
 communities across North Carolina. Featuring historical photographs\, cont
 emporary images\, artworks from the Gregg Museum collection including a ha
 ndmade guitar by Freeman Vines\, and ephemera from community partners\, th
 e exhibition reflects on place\, memory\, creativity\, and spiritual resil
 ience across generations. Through stories of triumph and adversity\, Commu
 nity Stories honors the ways Black Americans have sustained and uplifted t
 heir communities through family\, entrepreneurship\, cultural expression\,
  and soulful imagination\, while inspiring future generations.
GEO:35.784925;-78.661662
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining
 -north-carolinas-black-heritage
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
