X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/introduction-to-focus-groups-3506"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261128T073145Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54427482151284
DTSTART:20270413T140000Z
DTEND:20270414T040000Z
DESCRIPTION:Focus groups are commonly used to capture rich information abou
 t attitudes and beliefs. This class will prepare prospective students to o
 rganize and moderate focus groups. Students will learn the most appropriat
 e uses of focus groups\, how to segment and recruit audiences\, how to dev
 elop a moderator’s guide\, and how to moderate focus groups. The class w
 ill be supplemented with real-life examples and hands-on exercises.\n\nReg
 istration and fee (refundable for UNCCH students upon attendance of course
 ) are required for Zoom link access.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Introduction to Focus Groups
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/introduction-to-focus-groups-3
 506
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
